---
title: Bucket collection
layout: home
description: Things to do — grouped, checked off, and left on the page once they are done, because a list that deletes what you achieved is a to-do list and not a record of anything.
eyebrow: Collections · Bucket list
source: src/components/life.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Bucket list · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-wrap-wide im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
	<header class="im-collhead im-collhead-patterned">
			<span class="im-collhead-art im-bg-zigzag" style="--im-art: var(--im-c-bucket)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
		<p class="im-eyebrow">Bucket list</p>
		<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Things to do, and things done</h1>
		<p class="im-collhead-text">Written down because a thing that is not written down is a mood, not a plan. The left column is the list. The right column is the reason the left column is worth keeping.</p>
		<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>{{demo.wishlist.length}} in total</span><span>5 done</span><span>2 booked</span><span>Since 2023</span></p>
	</header>

	<div class="im-collbar">
		<div class="im-collbar-filters" role="group" aria-label="Which kind" data-im-filter="#board">
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="all" aria-current="page">Everything</button>
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="Water" aria-current="false">{{icon "volume-2"}}Water</button>
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="Cold" aria-current="false">{{icon "moon"}}Cold</button>
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="Air" aria-current="false">{{icon "arrow-up"}}Air</button>
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="Ground" aria-current="false">{{icon "route"}}Ground</button>
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="Work" aria-current="false">{{icon "briefcase"}}Work</button>
		</div>
		<p class="im-progress-field" style="min-width: 12rem"><span>Done</span><output>5 of {{demo.wishlist.length}}</output><span class="im-progress" role="progressbar" aria-label="Done" aria-valuenow="42" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" style="--im-value: .42"></span></p>
	</div>

	<div class="im-bucketboard" id="board">
		<section class="im-bucketcol" data-side="todo" aria-labelledby="b-todo">
			<header class="im-bucketcol-head">
				<h2 class="im-bucketcol-title" id="b-todo">{{icon "square-dashed"}}Still to do</h2>
				<span class="im-bucketcol-count">7</span>
				<p class="im-bucketcol-text">Two of them are booked, which is the only difference between a list and a wish.</p>
			</header>
			<ul class="im-buckets">
				{{#each demo.wishlist}}{{#unless state}}
				<li class="im-bucket" data-facet="{{group}}">
					<span class="im-bucket-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<p class="im-bucket-title"><span class="im-kind" data-kind="bucket" style="margin-right: .375rem">{{icon "square-dashed"}}To do</span>{{title}}</p>
					<p class="im-bucket-note">{{note}}</p>
					<p class="im-bucket-when">{{when}}</p>
				</li>
				{{/unless}}{{/each}}
				{{#each demo.wishlist}}{{#match state "=" "booked"}}
				<li class="im-bucket" data-state="booked" data-facet="{{group}}">
					<span class="im-bucket-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<p class="im-bucket-title"><span class="im-kind" data-kind="bucket" style="margin-right: .375rem">{{icon "square-dashed"}}To do</span>{{title}}</p>
					<p class="im-bucket-note">{{note}}</p>
					<p class="im-bucket-when">{{when}}</p>
				</li>
				{{/match}}{{/each}}
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="im-bucketcol" data-side="done" aria-labelledby="b-done">
			<header class="im-bucketcol-head">
				<h2 class="im-bucketcol-title" id="b-done">{{icon "circle-check"}}Done</h2>
				<span class="im-bucketcol-count">5</span>
				<p class="im-bucketcol-text">Each one gets a picture and a paragraph, because doing it is what turns a sentence into something worth reading.</p>
			</header>
			<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .75rem">
				{{#each demo.wishlist}}{{#match state "=" "done"}}
				<article class="im-done" data-facet="{{group}}">
					<span class="im-done-media"><img src="{{lookup ../demo.shots shot}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
					<p class="im-done-when">{{when}}</p><p><span class="im-kind" data-kind="experience">{{icon "circle-check"}}Done</span></p>
					<h3 class="im-done-title"><a href="/collections/experience/page/">{{title}}</a></h3>
					<p class="im-done-text">{{text}}</p>
				</article>
				{{/match}}{{/each}}
			</div>
			<p><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="/collections/experience/">{{icon "arrow-right"}}Every one of them, in full</a></p>
		</section>
	</div>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>A checklist, not a shopping list</h2>
		<p>The state is the whole point, so it is the first thing on every row: an empty ring for someday, an accent ring for booked, a filled tick for done. It is the same vocabulary a <a href="/navigation/curriculum/">course lesson</a> uses, because it is the same idea — a thing you have or have not got to yet.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th><code>data-state</code></th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><em>none</em></td><td>Someday. An empty ring, and the date column says so.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>booked</code></td><td>It is happening: an accent ring, and a real date.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>done</code></td><td>A filled tick, the title struck through but <strong>still legible</strong>, and the date in the success colour.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>Leave the done ones on the page</h2>
		<p>A list that deletes an item the moment it happens is a to-do list. Leaving it — struck through, dated, and linked to the <a href="/collections/experience/">experience</a> it became — is what turns the page into a record of a life rather than a set of intentions.</p>
		<p>That link is the only navigation the collection needs. A done row goes to what happened; the experience page links back to the line it came from.</p>

		<h2>Rules</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Group them by something real.</strong> Water, cold, distance — not "high priority", which is a project-management word and means nothing on a list like this.</li>
			<li><strong>"Someday" is an honest answer.</strong> A made-up date on every line makes the two real dates worth nothing.</li>
			<li><strong>Nine is a list. Forty is a fantasy.</strong></li>
			<li><strong>No prices.</strong> This is not a <a href="/collections/uses/">wish-to-buy</a> page; it is a wish-to-do one.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
